{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979155016,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d36effeOhlnHzaXDGcEx2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_PebxEJ4MoUVUlD8jDdoer9yb","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"perioste","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl","include":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl"},"output":"Found 5 matches\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 13395: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"VSAO:curator\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001039 \"Osteoblast that is terminally differentiated, located adjacent to acellular or cellular bone tissue within periosteum, and is capable of mineralizing the matrix.\")\n\n  Line 13402: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"VSAO:curator\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001040 \"Osteoblast that is non-terminally differentiated and located in cellular bone tissue or under the periosteum in acellular bone.\")\n\n  Line 22605: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007001 \"Cell that has the potential to form a skeletal cell type (e.g. cells in periosteum, cells in marrow) and produce extracellular matrix (often mineralized) and skeletal tissue (often mineralized).\")\n\n  Line 25599: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34280086\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.12.07.570646\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020016 \"A tissue-specific stem cell with long-term self-renewal capacity that is restricted to generating bone, cartilage, and stromal cell lineages. This cell is primarily located in the growth plate (resting zone), periosteum, and subchondral bone regions, and is marked by high clonogenicity and robust multipotent differentiation potential in both osteogenic and chondrogenic lineages. Distinctively, ocSSC lacks adipogenic capacity, distinguishing it from other mesenchymal stem cell populations.\")\n\n  Line 25669: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29985449\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34137454\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020022 \"A post-proliferative chondrocyte in the prehypertrophic zone of the cartilage tissue, located between the proliferative and hypertrophic zones. This cell is characterised by increased cell volume and expression of Indian Hedgehog (Ihh), PTH1R, and Runx2/3 in both humans and mice (Hallett et al., 2021). It coordinates the PTHrP-Ihh feedback loop that regulates chondrocyte differentiation and functions as a signalling hub for communication between proliferative chondrocytes, hypertrophic chondrocytes, and periosteal osteoblasts (Hallett et al., 2021).\")\n","metadata":{"matches":5,"truncated":false},"title":"perioste","time":{"start":1778979154958,"end":1778979155014}},"id":"prt_e336bac09001PKosRrILrwJIF2","sessionID":"ses_1cc94d36effeOhlnHzaXDGcEx2","messageID":"msg_e336b936a001dTZCZy1dkH8ih1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979155021,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d36effeOhlnHzaXDGcEx2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_SIbrNQz0tjRa0h9p4EtEnTjh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"Runx2|Sox9|Col2a1|Col1a1","path":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl","include":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl"},"output":"Found 2 matches\n/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl:\n  Line 25669: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29985449\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34137454\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020022 \"A post-proliferative chondrocyte in the prehypertrophic zone of the cartilage tissue, located between the proliferative and hypertrophic zones. This cell is characterised by increased cell volume and expression of Indian Hedgehog (Ihh), PTH1R, and Runx2/3 in both humans and mice (Hallett et al., 2021). It coordinates the PTHrP-Ihh feedback loop that regulates chondrocyte differentiation and functions as a signalling hub for communication between proliferative chondrocytes, hypertrophic chondrocytes, and periosteal osteoblasts (Hallett et al., 2021).\")\n\n  Line 34272: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31320652\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32530882\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36758341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Theca_externa\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052013 \"A specialized theca cell that forms the outer layer of the theca surrounding the ovarian follicle, appearing at the antral follicle. Originating from progenitor theca cells, theca externa cell is characterized by its fibroblast-like appearance and primarily function to provide structural support to the developing follicle. This cell produces collagen fibers and extracellular matrix components such as Col1a1 and Col1a2.\")\n","metadata":{"matches":2,"truncated":false},"title":"Runx2|Sox9|Col2a1|Col1a1","time":{"start":17