{"type":"text","timestamp":1778979193918,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d36effeOhlnHzaXDGcEx2","part":{"id":"prt_e336c36f4001eYZh762ksvjqSj","messageID":"msg_e336c2d30001waoDcz0tjetn1P","sessionID":"ses_1cc94d36effeOhlnHzaXDGcEx2","type":"text","text":"I’m editing `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl` now. The change will be minimal: one new class stanza with the issue link, PMID-backed definition, species restriction to mouse, periosteum location, contributor ORCID, date, and creator metadata.","time":{"start":1778979190516,"end":1778979193916}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979193995,"sessionID":"ses_1cc94d36effeOhlnHzaXDGcEx2","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_zWesNP91xEoBhAZof9c6BQdv","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","offset":25716,"limit":30},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/src/ontology/cl-edit.owl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n25716: # Class: obo:CL_0020026 (alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-transient (Mmus))\n25717: \n25718: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020026 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype found in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to decreases in light intensity. It is characterized by a large soma, a broad dendritic arbor that stratifies within sublamina a of the inner plexiform layer, and rapid OFF-transient firing kinetics that decay even during sustained stimulation (Krieger et al., 2017). Functionally, it corresponds to G8 in the Baden functional classification (Baden et al., 2016; Goetz et al., 2022) and C45 in the Tran transcriptomic atlas (Tran et al., 2019), and it is considered the evolutionary ortholog of the primate OFF Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). This cell type acts as a detector of rapidly approaching dark objects and contributes to innate defensive responses by encoding looming stimuli (Münch et al., 2009). It exhibits a distinctive molecular signature by its expression of Brn3c (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\n25719: AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020026 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3493\")\n25720: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020026 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n25721: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020026 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n25722: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_0020026 \"2025-12-05T11:29:19Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n25723: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020026 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-t\")\n25724: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020026 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\n25725: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020026 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-transient (Mmus)\")\n25726: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 obo:CL_0004117)\n25727: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 obo:CL_4023033)\n25728: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))\n25729: \n25730: # Class: obo:CL_0020027 (alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-transient (Mmus))\n25731: \n25732: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020027 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to increases in light intensity. It possesses the large soma and expansive dendritic field characteristic of alpha RGCs (Krieger et al., 2017). This cell exhibits a brief, fast-decaying burst of firing at the onset of light increments and contributes to motion detection for luminance increases, forming the ON-branch of the transient magnocellular-like pathway (Krieger et al., 2017; Hahn et al., 2023). Functionally, it corresponds to cluster G19 and aligns transcriptomically with cluster C41 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019). It is orthologous to the primate ON Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). Molecularly, it expresses Spp1, Smi32, and Brn3b, but lacks Brn3a, Brn3c, and Calbindin (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\n25733: AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_0020027 obo:NCBITaxon_10090)\n25734: AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020027 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\n25735: AnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020027 \"GitHub Copilot\")\n25736: AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_0020027 \"2025-12-05T00:00:00Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n25737: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"C41\")\n25738: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"G19\")\n25739: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020027 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-t\")\n25740: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020027 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\n25741: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020027 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-transient (Mmus)\")\n25742: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020027 obo:CL_0004117)\n25743: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020027 obo:CL_4023032)\n25744: SubClassOf(obo:CL_0020027 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))\n25745: \n\n(Showing lines 25716-25745 of 35584. Use offset=25746 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Class: obo:CL_0020026 (alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-transient (Mmus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020026 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype found in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to decreases in light intensity. It is characterized by a large soma, a broad dendritic arbor that stratifies within sublamina a of the inner plexiform layer, and rapid OFF-transient firing kinetics that decay even during sustained stimulation (Krieger et al., 2017). Functionally, it corresponds to G8 in the Baden functional classification (Baden et al., 2016; Goetz et al., 2022) and C45 in the Tran transcriptomic atlas (Tran et al., 2019), and it is considered the evolutionary ortholog of the primate OFF Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). This cell type acts as a detector of rapidly approaching dark objects and contributes to innate defensive responses by encoding looming stimuli (Münch et al., 2009). It exhibits a distinctive molecular signature by its expression of Brn3c (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0020026 \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3493\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020026 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020026 \"GitHub Copilot\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:creation_date obo:CL_0020026 \"2025-12-05T11:29:19Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0020026 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-t\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0020026 \"The G-type nomenclature used here refers specifically to the functional classification of mouse retinal ganglion cells introduced by Baden and colleagues, and is distinct from earlier G-based schemes used for rabbit or other species. Readers should be aware that the same letter–number labels (e.g., \\\"G1\\\", \\\"G2\\\") have been applied in different historical contexts to different animals and criteria (functional vs. morphological), so cross-species or cross-era comparisons of \\\"G\\\" names should not be assumed equivalent without explicit mapping in the primary literature.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0020026 \"alpha retinal ganglion cell OFF-transient (Mmus)\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 obo:CL_0004117)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 obo:CL_4023033)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020026 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))\n\n# Class: obo:CL_0020027 (alpha retinal ganglion cell ON-transient (Mmus))\n\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020027 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to increases in light intensity. It possesses the large soma and expansive dendritic field characteristic of alpha RGCs (Krieger et al., 2017). This cell exhibits a brief, fast-decaying burst of firing at the onset of light increments and contributes to motion detection for luminance increases, forming the ON-branch of the transient magnocellular-like pathway (Krieger et al., 2017; Hahn et al., 2023). Functionally, it corresponds to cluster G19 and aligns transcriptomically with cluster C41 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019). It is orthologous to the primate ON Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). Molecularly, it expresses Spp1, Smi32, and Brn3b, but lacks Brn3a, Brn3c, and Calbindin (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_0020027 obo:NCBITaxon_10090)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_0020027 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5507-2103>)\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:creator obo:CL_0020027 \"GitHub Copilot\")","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"title":"src/ontology/cl-edit.owl","time":{"start":1778979193871,"end":1778979193992}},"id":"prt_e336c44080015p7m8qe7OEbBtG","sessionID":"ses_1cc94d36effeOhlnHzaXDGcEx2","messageID":"msg_e336c2d30001waoDcz0tjetn1P"}}
